# The repositories that belong on every machine you work from: one per line.
#
#   <name>  <repository>  [branch]
#
# This is a list of what should be present, not a description of one machine
# handing work to another. `roost projects` brings the machine it runs on up
# to the list — run it on the stand and on your workstation alike, and both
# end up with the same set of checkouts. The shared state is the repository,
# not either machine.
#
# Nothing here is ever overwritten: a checkout with uncommitted work is named
# and skipped, and so is a name already taken by a directory that is not a
# checkout at all.
#
# The name is also the directory under project_dir and the tmux session
# suffix, so `roost-session start isearch` finds it.
#
# A project's Claude settings and CLAUDE.md ride inside its own repository —
# nothing extra to configure here. What does not ride along is anything
# gitignored, secrets in particular.
#
# Leave the branch out to follow the repository's own default branch.
#
# isearch  https://git.example/hitromudr/isearch.git
# sorter   https://github.com/hitromudr/sorter.git  develop
